oxc-node is a fast and developer-friendly set of Node.js development
tools built on top of Oxc, the Rust-based JavaScript and TypeScript
toolchain. Oxc provides shared compiler infrastructure and end-user
tools for parsing, transforming, linting, formatting, minifying,
and resolving JavaScript/TypeScript code. Its main components include
Oxlint for linting, Oxfmt for formatting, the Parser for building
ASTs, the Transformer for TypeScript/JSX/modern JavaScript compilation,
the Minifier for production output, and the Resolver for module
resolution.

Within that ecosystem, oxc-node focuses specifically on the Node.js
development runtime. Its current main package, @oxc-node/core,
provides a transformer and Node.js register hook, allowing Node.js
projects to use Oxc's fast transformation pipeline during
development. In other words, Oxc is the broader compiler/tooling
stack, while oxc-node is the Node.js integration layer that brings
Oxc's speed and transformation capabilities directly into Node.js
workflows.
